  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 114 PM CDT Wed Oct 14 2026\n\n...Synopsis...\n\nWidespread stratus deck continues to linger across the Northern \nPlains and Upper Midwest this afternoon, keeping temperatures in the \nlow to mid 40s thus far today. Upper flow is nearly zonal, but will \nbe transitioning to southwest this evening and overnight before \nshifting to the northwest late Thursday evening. Very light \nprecipitation is possible along a cold front Thursday afternoon and \nevening, mainly from the Red River Valley eastward into northwest \nMinnesota. Breezy northwest winds pick up early Thursday morning and \npersist through much of the day. The strongest pressure gradients \nshift eastward overnight into Friday morning with weak, transient, \nridging bringing warmer temperatures into the area for Saturday and \nSunday.\n\n...Breezy Northwest Winds Thursday...\n\nSustained northwest winds of 20-30 mph are possible Thursday with \ngusts upwards of 40-45 mph. This will be in response to a fast \nmoving cold front and strong pressure rises on the western side of \nthe frontal passage. There is still some uncertainty surrounding \ncloud cover, which could limit mixing during the afternoon and \nevening and slightly reduce the potential max wind gusts. At this \ntime, the signal is consistently strong, however, with generally \nmoderate to high confidence in the possibility of Advisory \nlevel winds.\n\n...Freezing Temperatures Possible Friday Night...\n\nGuidance continues to bring colder air into the area following \nThursday's cold front. Low temperatures Friday morning are expected \nto be in the lower 30s, but with lingering cloud cover. A better \nchance of upper 20s and low 30s will be Friday night into Saturday \nmorning as cloud cover is expected to diminish by midday Friday.",
